            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0145" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1005: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-29">June 29, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1486. Reference Department’s 1418, June 26. Philippine citizens as American
                    nationals are of course to be accommodated on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi>
                    <pb facs="0146" n="137" xml:id="pg137"/> the same as American citizens. However,
                    loans are not authorized for them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
